The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
irqd->domain = irq_domain_add_linear(lp->dev->of_node, LP8788_INT_MAX, &lp8788_domain_ops, irqd);
if (!irqd->domain) {
    dev_err(lp->dev, "failed to add irq domain err\n");
    return -EINVAL;
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because if `irq_domain_add_linear()` succeeds but subsequent operations (like `request_threaded_irq()`) fail, the allocated IRQ domain is not removed, leading to resource leaks. This lack of cleanup can cause memory and resource management issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
+		irq_domain_remove(lp->irqdm);
```
```c
+	if (lp->irqdm)
+		irq_domain_remove(lp->irqdm);
```
Reason:
The fix involves adding calls to `irq_domain_remove()` in both the error handling path of `lp8788_irq_init()` and in `lp8788_irq_exit()`. This ensures that if an error occurs after successfully adding the IRQ domain, it is properly removed, preventing resource leaks and ensuring better resource management.

